# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values.
#   cp .env.example .env
# .env is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# The file has to exist for the app to build, because pubspec.yaml lists it as
# an asset — that is how flutter_dotenv reads it. An empty .env is fine.

# --- NEVER ship or deploy ----------------------------------------------------
# The AI service powers Nook's destination, category, summary and coordinate
# detection, and writes the Explore Itinerary plans. The key is billable:
# anyone can read a value compiled into a web build and spend your credit, so it
# is deliberately NOT a repository secret and never reaches the deployed site.
#
# Leave this blank and Nook falls back to its sample extractor and its sample
# planner, which is exactly what the published GitHub Pages build does — and it
# says so on screen.
# Create a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Leave blank and Nook uses the fast tier it pins itself. Set an id
# here only to pin a different one, e.g. claude-haiku-4-5-20251001.
CLAUDE_MODEL=

# Optional, and separate from the Anthropic key.
#
# oEmbed gives Nook a YouTube video's title and channel and nothing else — it
# has no description field at all. The description is where the detail lives:
# the cafe names, the addresses, the prices. With a YouTube Data API key Nook
# fetches it and hands it to the model, which is the difference between "Kyoto"
# and five named cafes.
#
# Free tier, no billing account. Enable "YouTube Data API v3" at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/youtube.googleapis.com
# Leave blank and extraction works from the title alone.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# ── Instagram and Facebook ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional, and the only way these two can be read at all.
#
# Both platforms served public oEmbed until October 2020 and then withdrew it.
# Since then a post's caption, author and thumbnail come only from the Graph
# API, which needs a Meta app. Without this, an Instagram or Facebook link
# extracts from its URL alone — Nook says so in the prompt rather than letting
# the model invent a caption it cannot see.
#
# To fill it in: create an app at https://developers.facebook.com/apps,
# add the "oEmbed Read" feature, then use APP_ID|CLIENT_TOKEN — the app id and
# the client token from Settings → Advanced, joined by a pipe.
#
# YouTube and TikTok need none of this; their oEmbed is still public.
FACEBOOK_TOKEN=
